# counter harness. One force call is one clean energy and gradient.
# Noise is added after the call. A repeated coordinate keeps that sample.
# The index uses the clean Hessian. Six rigid modes are removed.
# A curvature is negative only below -max(force_norm, 1e-8*||H||_F, 1e-6).
# Energy and Kabsch RMSD are not applied: the problem file has no per-start reference.
# Default profile. The stop is the noise-aware force norm, and at positive sigma the clean energy over the last window. The index is the clean Hessian with the rigid-mode rule. LD_LBFGS, LD_VAR2, and LD_SLSQP scale the objective by 0.2 divided by the initial force norm. LD_TNEWTON_PRECOND_RESTART recenters a coordinate box of half-width 0.2. LD_MMA keeps the library defaults.
